  "description": "QUVRIK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H78 Ho4 N6 O20,2(C3 H7 N1 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.448-3.840 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.28-110.97°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [HoIII4(μ3-OH)2(L)4(piv)2(DMF)2]·2DMF (C78H92Ho4N8O22; L = 2-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenylsalicylaldiminate; piv = pivalate). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ho(III).",
